content.text:
This is quite complex syntax. Can it be simlpified? let mut root = VStack::new()
            .children(vec![
                Box::new(Text::new("a")),
                Box::new(HStack::new().children(vec![Box::new(Text::new("b"))])),
            ])
            .build();

Good instinct — that nesting is noisy. The complexity comes from four things: `VStack::new()`, `.children(vec![...])`, `Box::new(...)` for trait objects, and `.build()`. All are eliminable. Here are the options.

## Option A: `macro_rules!` stacks + free `text()`/`spacer()` functions (Recommended)

Zero new dependencies, works in `no_std`. The macros absorb the boxing and `vec!`/`.children()` boilerplate internally:

```rust
// pathland-view/src/lib.rs
#[macro_export]
macro_rules! vstack {
    ($($child:expr),* $(,)?) => {
        $crate::VStack::new().children($crate::vec![$($crate::Box::new($child)),*])
    };
}
#[macro_export]
macro_rules! hstack { /* same, HStack */ }

pub fn text(content: &str) -> Text { Text::new(content) }
pub fn spacer() -> Spacer { Spacer }
```

Result:

```rust
let mut root = vstack![
    text("a"),
    hstack![text("b")],
]
.padding(8.0)
.build();
```

- `Box::new`, `.children(vec![...])`, `.new()` all gone; modifiers still chain (`vstack![...].spacing(4.0)`).
- `hstack![text("b")]` inside `vstack!` just works — the inner expansion is a `HStack`, boxed by the outer macro.
- Needs `pub use alloc::{boxed::Box, vec};` at the crate root for macro hygiene.
- Not SwiftUI-literal, but close.

## Option B: Proc-macro result builder (true SwiftUI literal)

```rust
vstack {
    text("a")
    hstack { text("b") }
}
```

- Requires a new **proc-macro crate** (syn/quote deps, a whole package, export both), no_std unaffected since macros are compile-time. Heaviest option; probably premature for the POC.

## Optional add-on: fold `.build()` + `assign_ids`

The end-of-expression `.build()` is a one-time cost (you build once, then mutate+emit). If you want to drop it too, add a convenience on `Engine`:

```rust
engine.emit_view(&vstack![text("a")], &mut guest);
// build() + assign_ids(&mut node, &mut 1) + emit() in one call
```

Note: pre-order re-assignment is only safe for first build — on subsequent emissions the app mutates the retained tree and calls `engine.emit` directly (ids must stay stable for diffing). So this only removes ceremony for the initial tree.

---

My recommendation: **Option A** (macros + free functions), which gets the example down to ~5 clean lines with zero deps. Keep `.build()`/`assign_ids` as-is for now.

